<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacques Cassard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1679">1679</a>–<a href="/years/1740">1740</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacques Cassard was a French naval officer and privateer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> he led a squadron that raided Portuguese, English and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonies in 1712, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>, where the planters paid a heavy ransom to save their estates. A quarrel with the authorities later led to his imprisonment, and he died in the fortress of Joux.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacques-cassard.jpg" alt="Jacques Cassard" width="320" height="499" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierren · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacques_Cassard-Pierren_img_3095.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
